ins or  to the coast so you can kind of have a  kind of fun dual  vacation they are great properties with  availability right downtown like the  portland marriott and then i also want  to mention atlanta so if you're looking  for something fun with the families  atlanta flights under 200 round trips so  much to do with the families in the city  nice mild weather you have the college  football hall of fame the botanic  gardens the aquarium there's actually  three national parks right around  atlanta  it's a great city of neighborhoods if  you're looking for something a little  luxurious stay in buckhead you have the  jw marriott there that has butler  service afternoon tea in their piazza  pool so  lots to do there and really affordable  still now i know this may be asking for  too much but are there still ways to  actually save this late in the game  yeah that's a great question a few  things that you should consider number  one is with flight most people actually  leave on saturdays and sundays for  spring break their kids get out of  school on friday and that's when they  head out so if you can be flexible and  travel monday through thursday you're  really going to find better availability  and some decent prices to some of these  off markets for your flight um also like  we're doing now kind of think like a  contrarian if everyone's going to the  hot spots where can you go so instead of  beach think about desert destinations  right look at some of these big cities  that aren't going to be into their high  season until summer so that's really  kind of a way to save when you're  looking for  places to go this late in the game wow  such great advice great destinations  thank you so much for your expertise  janine we really appreciate it kendall  i'm going to send it back to you
 

